claim.claim-text:
displaying, on a display, a two-dimensional array of input regions, wherein each input region of a subset of the input regions corresponds to a respective hiragana character of a first set of hiragana characters, each hiragana character of the first set represents a combination of a respective consonant with a common vowel, and the display comprises a touch panel configured to detect a touch to any of the input regions;
in response to detecting a touch to an input region of the subset of the input regions that corresponds to a hiragana character of the first set of hiragana characters representing a combination of a given consonant with the common vowel, displaying an arrangement of hiragana characters in which a plurality of associated hiragana characters are displayed with the hiragana character to which the touched input region corresponds, each associated hiragana character being displayed at a different respective display position relative to a display position of the hiragana character to which the touched input region corresponds, and each associated hiragana character representing a combination of the given consonant with a different respective vowel; and
in response to detecting that the detected touch has moved in a direction corresponding to the display position of one of the associated hiragana characters relative to the display position of the hiragana character to which the touched input region corresponds, and has subsequently been released, determining that the corresponding one of the associated hiragana characters has been inputted.
